{
  "body_human_readable": "### Tesla's 2024 Deliveries Mark First Annual Decline in Over a Decade\n\nIn 2024, Tesla delivered a total of 1,789,226 vehicles, experiencing a slight decrease of 1.11% from the previous year. This marks the first time in over a decade that the electric vehicle giant has seen a year-over-year decline in deliveries.\n\nA detailed look at the year reveals a progressive increase in deliveries each quarter:\n*   **First Quarter:** 386,810 vehicles\n*   **Second Quarter:** Approximately 444,000 vehicles\n*   **Third Quarter:** Approximately 463,000 vehicles\n*   **Fourth Quarter:** Over 495,000 vehicles\n\nThe majority of the vehicles delivered in 2024 were the Model 3 and Model Y, accounting for 1,704,093 of the total. The remaining 85,133 deliveries were of other models, including the recently launched Cybertruck.\n\nDespite the slight annual dip, the fourth quarter of 2024 set a new record for Tesla with the highest number of deliveries and energy storage deployments in a single quarter. The company produced a total of 1,773,443 vehicles throughout the year.",
